SPDX-FileNotice: retrods local patch, not part of upstream libretro-common.

Use a bare `static __inline__` instead of `static INLINE`.

These headers write `static INLINE ...`, which requires INLINE to be a *bare*
inline specifier. Cores routinely redefine INLINE for their own code - fmsx does
`#undef INLINE` + `#define INLINE static inline`, and Genesis-Plus-GX ends up
with C99 `inline` depending on include order - and libretro-common then either
fails to compile (`static static inline`) or emits duplicate globals.

Replacing the macro use with the specifier directly makes libretro-common
independent of whatever a core does with INLINE.

Applied with: patch -p1 < patches/libretro-common/0001-inline-specifier.patch
